(go/type WriteScheduler "WriteScheduler is the interface implemented by HTTP/2 write schedulers.\nMethods are never called concurrently.\n" (interface



    (^{:doc "OpenStream opens a new stream in the write scheduler.\nIt is illegal to call this with streamID=0 or with a streamID that is\nalready open -- the call may panic.\n"} OpenStream [^uint32 streamID ^OpenStreamOptions options])




    (^{:doc "CloseStream closes a stream in the write scheduler. Any frames queued on\nthis stream should be discarded. It is illegal to call this on a stream\nthat is not open -- the call may panic.\n"} CloseStream [^uint32 streamID])





    (^{:doc "AdjustStream adjusts the priority of the given stream. This may be called\non a stream that has not yet been opened or has been closed. Note that\nRFC 7540 allows PRIORITY frames to be sent on streams in any state. See:\nhttps://tools.ietf.org/html/rfc7540#section-5.1\n"} AdjustStream [^uint32 streamID ^PriorityParam priority])




    (^{:doc "Push queues a frame in the scheduler. In most cases, this will not be\ncalled with wr.StreamID()!=0 unless that stream is currently open. The one\nexception is RST_STREAM frames, which may be sent on idle or closed streams.\n"} Push [^FrameWriteRequest wr])





    (^{:doc "Pop dequeues the next frame to write. Returns false if no frames can\nbe written. Frames with a given wr.StreamID() are Pop'd in the same\norder they are Push'd, except RST_STREAM frames. No frames should be\ndiscarded except by CloseStream.\n"} Pop [] :results [^FrameWriteRequest wr ^bool ok])))



